<header><p class="eyebrow">THE GAUCHO WORLD · ENGLISH CULTURAL RESEARCH</p><h1>What Is a Payada? Gaucho Poetry, Guitar and Improvised Song</h1><p class="deck">In a payada, words become a public performance. Singers use verse and melody to tell stories, answer one another and sometimes compete. This living tradition offers a way into the poetic world that José Hernández created in Martín Fierro.</p></header>
